In My estimation, the quality of StackExchange sites/pages has declined
substantially over time to the point I wouldn't bother but would recommend
either Facebook or Reddit instead.

On Tuesday, February 17, 2015, Emrakul <noahsutsmo@gmail.com> wrote:

> 'Ello!
>
> I'm looking to create a Stack Exchange site for lojban language and
> culture. Currently, the site is in the *Definition* phase, which means it
> needs these things to continue:
>
>    - Post example questions! - These are things like "What's changed
>    since The Complete Lojban?" or "What resources are available to learn
>    xorlo?", et cetera.
>    - Vote up good example questions! - Pick five questions under a score
>    of 10 that you like, and upvote 'em. We need 40 posts with 10 votes to
>    continue.
>    - If you'd like, follow the proposal!
>
> Here's the link to the proposal.
> <http://area51.stackexchange.com/proposals/83133/jbobau-joi-jboceu-lojban-language-and-culture?referrer=m6cRPv027d45-WqLeTqQlw2> It
> needs a certain number of all of these to continue. *Example questions
> and votes are particularly important. *The progress toward the next phase
> has been wholly remarkable, given it's only been three days. (Also, don't
> worry about spam. If I recall correctly, Stack Exchange only sends you two
> or three emails total, and that's just to let you know when the proposal
> advances to the next phase.)
>
> Stack Exchange is a Q&A platform which is search engine-optimized and
> designed pretty much for exactly this purpose: recording questions and
> answers on a topic, and indexing them for future readers.
>
> Mildly confused? Here's a uitki artile!
> <http://mw.lojban.org/papri/Lojban.SE>
>
> If you have any questions/comments/suggestions, feel free to ask here, and
> I'll do what I can to field them.
>
> I tried to keep this short, but it's still too long. Oh well!
>
> ++N
